{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>To a clean place.</b> Since outside the city there is a place prepared for uncleanness — to cast stricken stones and for graves — it was necessary to say 'outside this camp' — which is outside the city — that the place must be clean." "<b>Outside the camp.</b> Outside three camps; and the eternal House [the Temple] is outside the city, as our Sages explained in tractate Yoma (68a) and in Sanhedrin (42b)." "<b>To the ash-heap.</b> The place where they pour the ash removed from the altar, as stated ״וְהוֹצִיא אֶת הַדֶּשֶׁן אֶל מִחוּץ לַמַּחֲנֶה״ (Leviticus 6)." "<b>At the ash-heap it shall be burnt.</b> For there is no need for Scripture to say it — rather, to teach that even if there is no ash there (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:09.680996545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}